# Testing & QA Rules

Always run the checks available for the area you changed. Fix failures before finishing.

## Frontend (`cd frontend`)

```bash
npm run typecheck   # tsc --noEmit
npm run lint        # next lint
npm run build       # production build — run for routing/config changes
```

No unit test suite is configured. Manually verify affected pages in the browser.

## Backend (`cd backend`)

```bash
source venv/bin/activate
python manage.py test                    # Django test runner
python manage.py check                   # system checks
python manage.py makemigrations --check  # after model changes
```

Smoke scripts (when touching IAP or deploy):

```bash
python backend/scripts/check_iap_production.py
```

Root-level `test_ai_copilot.py` — run only when changing `ai_copilot`.

## Mobile (`cd mobile`)

```bash
npm run typecheck      # tsc --noEmit
npm run test:api       # API smoke test against configured base URL
npm run test:web       # Playwright (web wrapper tests)
npm run test:e2e       # Maestro native smoke (requires simulator + dev build)
```

## QA checklist for UI changes

- [ ] Loading state visible while fetching
- [ ] Error state with readable message (use `getApiErrorMessage`)
- [ ] Empty state when list is `[]`
- [ ] Success state renders correct data from API
- [ ] Unauthenticated users redirected or blocked
- [ ] Admin-only pages reject non-admin users
- [ ] Mobile paid-access gates still work (`accessApi.checkPaidAccess`)

## When checks are unavailable

If lint/test tooling is missing for an area, state what you verified manually and what could not be run.
